---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;

const ideas = [
  {
    status: 'Research product v0.1 · prior art reviewed · test unvalidated',
    title: 'Expert-Attention Handoff Triage',
    summary: 'A formalism and benchmark proposal for allocating scarce expert review to candidate knowledge while measuring false negatives, expert-time yield, status bias and presentation sensitivity. Triage can route a claim but cannot confer authority.',
    href: internal('drafts/handoff-triage-formalism'),
  },
  {
    status: 'Draft v0.3 · deep lineage reviewed',
    title: 'Epistemic Handoff: Contribution, Authority and Uptake Under Cognitive Abundance',
    summary: 'A narrow, claim-sensitive handoff protocol built on contributorship, epistemic dependence, absorptive capacity, knowledge brokerage, innovation intermediaries, transactive memory and expert-evaluation research.',
    href: internal('drafts/epistemic-handoff'),
  },
  {
    status: 'Paper idea · operational extension',
    title: 'From Machine Discovery to Distributed Discovery: Provenance, Priority and Epistemic Authority in Human–AI Research',
    summary: 'Builds on computational-discovery and collective-discovery scholarship to represent problem framing, generation, significance recognition, validation, integration and realization without confusing novelty, priority, contribution or authority.',
    href: null,
  },
  {
    status: 'Paper idea · authority-layer extension',
    title: 'Credit Without Authority',
    summary: 'A claim-sensitive authority layer built on, rather than competing with, mature contributorship systems such as CRediT and guarantorship models.',
    href: null,
  },
  {
    status: 'Paper idea · absorptive-capacity extension',
    title: 'Epistemic Uptake Under Cognitive Abundance',
    summary: 'Asks how organizational and field-level absorptive/evaluative capacity behaves when machine cognition expands the supply of plausible candidate knowledge much faster than expert review and realization capacity.',
    href: null,
  },
  {
    status: 'Paper idea · expert-evaluation lineage',
    title: 'Allocating Expert Attention Under Candidate Abundance',
    summary: 'Starts from established evidence that expert juries can become scarce evaluation bottlenecks and asks how expert, crowd and machine triage can be combined without credential capture, pay-to-be-heard markets or destructive false negatives.',
    href: null,
  },
  {
    status: 'Deep-future paper · synthesis',
    title: 'The Human-Scale Epistemic Horizon',
    summary: 'Builds on computational-opacity and computer-assisted-proof literatures to examine the institutional consequences of reliable knowledge whose justification no individual human can fully survey.',
    href: null,
  },
  {
    status: 'Institutional research direction · existing intermediary lineage',
    title: 'Provenance-Aware Knowledge Orchestration',
    summary: 'Investigates whether existing knowledge-broker and innovation-intermediary models need new provenance, authority and routing machinery when candidate generation is machine-amplified. This replaces the looser “Epistemic Supply Chains” framing.',
    href: null,
  },
];
---
<Layout title="Drafts & Paper Ideas" description="Exploratory drafts and paper ideas in the Agalmic Research programme, including explicit lineage and novelty status.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Drafts & paper ideas</p>
      <h1>Ideas before they harden into claims.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A draft is an invitation to improve a question. A paper idea is not a novelty claim. Every item should survive an intellectual-lineage review before it enters the numbered sequence.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Working rule</p>
        <h2>Prior art is a ladder, not an embarrassment.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">If someone has already solved part of the problem, use their solution and move the research boundary.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Novelty is a conclusion of search, not a tone of voice.</strong></p></div>
        <p class="muted">The deep reviews have now reclassified machine discovery, knowledge routing, expert-attention bottlenecks and scarcity displacement as fields with substantial antecedents. The notebook therefore focuses increasingly on operational deltas and empirical questions.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('lineage')}>Read the lineage register →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Current notebook</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Drafts and adjacent papers.</h2>
          <p>Status labels describe both maturity and lineage. A mature antecedent narrows the question; it does not make the research direction worthless.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {ideas.map((idea, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{idea.href ? <a href={idea.href}>{idea.title}</a> : idea.title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{idea.summary}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{idea.status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Publication boundary</p>
        <h2>Open concepts, inspect machinery, search lineage first.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Conceptual openness remains the default, but public release should distinguish an established idea from a local extension. Detailed technical mechanisms still pass a separate publish / protect / continue-developing review where IP could matter.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('principles')}>Read the operating principles →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>